    "chunk_text": "In terms of weekly distribution within the month, the final full week of June proved to be the strongest period. The SLTDA report indicates that tourist arrivals between June 22 and 28 peaked at 32,519 visitors, driven primarily by strong daily inflows on June 26 and 27, which brought in 5,421 and 5,016 tourists respectively. This compared favourably with the first week of the month, which brought in 27,043 visitors, and the second week, which brought in 27,423 visitors.\n\nLooking at the picture for the first six months of 2026, India remains the undisputed leader with 293,683 arrivals, followed by the United Kingdom with 108,567 visitors. The Russian Federation holds the third spot overall with 77,349 tourists, despite not being in the top source markets for the specific month of June. China and Germany completed the cumulative top five source markets for the first half of the year, bringing in 76,171 and 69,758 tourists respectively."
