    "chunk_text": "Vedda Chief wants permanent solution to human-elephant conflict\n\nColombo, July 3 (Daily Mirror) -\u00a0Vedda Chief Wanaspathi Uruwarigelage Vannila Ettho\u2019s house had been ruined by a rogue elephant on Thursday night.\n\nVannila Ettho said the marauding jumbo that struted towards the house furiously pulled down the walls.\n\nThe people of his clan rushed to the scene and removed the debris of the house and commenced repairs.\n\nVannila Ettho pointed out that the human-elephant conflict was a serious issue affecting several parts of the country.\n\nHe stressed that steps should be taken to resolve it permanantly.\n\n\u201cThe threat of wild elephants has been escalating in Dambana and the surrounding villages. It is a waste of money to issue elephnat crackers. The maruading herds are not scared of elephnat crackers now. They are used to it,\u201d he further said."
