    "md5": "078bd9b507d4a4fda8dec8b865e54c3b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 853,
    "chunk_text": "Appeal Court dismisses Yoshitha Rajapaksa petition in money laundering case\n\nThe Court of Appeal yesterday dismissed a revision petition filed by Yoshitha Rajapaksa challenging the validity of a conspiracy charge brought against him in an ongoing money laundering case before the Colombo High Court.\n\nRajapaksa had sought a ruling that the conspiracy charge filed by the Attorney General under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act was not legally maintainable.\n\nHowever, a Bench comprising Justices Amal Ranaraja and Dr. Sumudu Premachandra rejected the petition, clearing the way for the conspiracy charge to proceed before the Colombo High Court.\n\nThe case stems from a money laundering indictment filed by the Attorney General against Rajapaksa. Following the Appeal Court\u2019s ruling, proceedings in the Colombo High Court are expected to continue."
