    "chunk_text": "The judging panel comprised respected industry and academic professionals, including Dr. Lasantha Malavige, Chairman of Lassana Group; Dr. Dilan Fernando, Director of SLIIT Innovate; Niresh Ratnagopal, Head of Programs at Hatch Works (Pvt) Ltd.; Rishan Sampath, Manager of Dilmah Conservation & Sustainability; along with Prof. Eranga Wijesinghe and Prof. Nathali Silva representing SLIIT.\n\nThe IGNITE Innovation Competition brought together around 80 participants from school and university categories, encouraging them to present commercially viable scientific solutions.In the university category, Team SilenceSpeak from SLIIT, led by Dineth Shawinda Samarakoon, won first place for their sign-language interpretation glove. In the school category, H.P. Dulja Sanuli Karunasekara from WP/GM/Yasodara Devi Balika Vidyalaya secured first place with a project on dengue mosquito larvae detection.\n\nCommenting on the initiative, Dr. Malitha Wijesundara, Pro Vice-Chancellor of the Faculty of Humanities and Sciences, stated:\u201cSciFest 2026 was created to help young minds see science beyond the classroom. By combining knowledge, creativity and entrepreneurship, we encourage students to think critically, develop practical solutions, and understand how innovation contributes to society and the economy.\u201d\n\nThe winners were awarded a total of Rs. 100,000 in cash prizes, along with medals, awards, and certificates in recognition of their outstanding achievements."
