    "md5": "4897aa0efc9157ac3b7f4f48af42f08d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1695,
    "chunk_text": "When the police were hot on the trail of the Zaharan gang, army intelligence operatives had asked them to call off the hunt. Not many in our Security Council had even visited Kattankudy which was the epicenter of the violence prone Islamists. Since I had done demographic research in Kattankudy many years earlier I was more familiar with the terrain and social conditions of the village than many of the top sleuths in the Security Council. I knew for instance that being traders, the Muslims of Kattankudy had an all island network of contacts. Zaharan could easily activate it in places like Mawanella, Kuliyapitiya and Gampola as it later transpired.\n\nIn this background of uncertainty and incompetence there began a move to support the candidature of Gotabaya Rajapaksa who had been an excellent manager of the war effort and the subsequent \u201cgreening\u201d of Colombo city. Since I was a personal friend of Gotabaya I proposed to the SLFP that we should support his candidature as his policies were the closest to ours. By this time the SLPP and SLFP were working together in the Parliamentary Opposition. Since the SLFP was dithering I decided to attend the opening of GR\u2019s campaign held in Shangri-La Hotel without bothering to get party approval.\n\nBasil seated me with the leaders of other parties affiliated to GR\u2019s campaign. This may have woken up the SLFP Central Committee because leaders like Nimal Siripala also demanded the freedom to join the GR campaign. Some others wanted to \u201cwait and see\u201d the outcome of the conflict that was brewing between Ranil and Sajith. I however threw myself into GR\u2019s campaign during the last few months remaining in my Parliamentary tenure."
  },
