    "chunk_text": "Local gold prices slightly down despite global rise\n\nColombo, July 4 (Daily Mirror) - Global gold prices continued to remain at elevated levels today (04), with the price of an ounce of gold increasing by 1.52 percent from the previous day to reach US$4,175.07.\n\nDespite the rise in international gold prices, local gold rates recorded a slight decline.\n\nAccording to the Sri Lanka Jewellers' Association, the price of a pound of 24-carat gold fell from Rs. 386,000 to Rs. 384,000 today.\n\nMeanwhile, the price of a pound of 22-carat gold also decreased, dropping from Rs. 355,100 to Rs. 353,300, the Association said."
