    "md5": "f82e227b63995285d898d8f9b7a1d7fc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1612,
    "chunk_text": "Eric J. De Silva\n\nEric J. De Silva who passed away recently at the age of nearly 90 was one of the outstanding public servants of his generation. Having joined the Ceylon Civil Service in 1960 he had a wide ranging career in Colombo and in the districts. Later in his career he specialized in the field of education, both locally and abroad, and working for the United Nations.\n\nEric had his early education at Mahinda College, Galle. He entered the University of Ceylon at Peradeniya in 1954, specializing in Economics, and obtaining an honours degree. He initially joined the Elections Department as an Assistant Elections Officer. In 1960 he entered the Ceylon Civil Service. One of his early assignments was with the Ministry of Defence and External affairs as Assistant Secretary. The permanent Secretary at the time was N.Q. Dias. Later, in the 1970s he worked as Senior Assistant Secretary in the same Ministry. The Prime Minister Mrs. Sirimavo Bandaranayaka who was also the Minister of Defence and External affairs had a high regard for him.\n\nEric served as Government Agent Trincomalee sometime later. This was at a time of civil disturbance in most parts of the island. District Coordinating Officers were appointed to many districts. In almost all cases these were Military officers, placed above the civilian Government Agents. The one exception was Eric who was appointed the Coordinating Officer for Trincomalee district. Most likely this was due to his previous experience in the Ministry of Defence. Eric later served as the Head of the Sri Lanka Institute of Development Administration (SLIDA)."
