    "chunk_text": "IChemC Annual Sessions 2026 inaugurated with focus on scientific excellence\n\nThe Annual Sessions 2026 of the Institute of Chemistry Ceylon (IChemC) commenced on June 26 with a formal inauguration ceremony attended by academics, researchers, students and invited guests.\n\nThe proceedings began with the arrival of guests and the singing of the National Anthem, followed by the welcome address and presidential speech delivered by IChemC President Prof. Emeritus H.M.K.K. Pathirana.\n\nThe ceremony also featured the presentation of awards, prizes, scholarships and certificates recognising outstanding achievements in chemistry Olympiads, BSc and GIC examinations, research activities and inter-university competitions.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Guest of Honour Udesha Bopitiya and Chief Guest Prof. Emeritus A.P. de Silva highlighted the importance of scientific excellence, research innovation and the role of chemistry in national development.\n\nProf. de Silva stressed the need to strengthen scientific inquiry and encourage young researchers to contribute to emerging global challenges through innovation and interdisciplinary collaboration.\n\nThe inauguration concluded with the vote of thanks delivered by IChemC President-Elect Prof. Emeritus Chandani Perera, who expressed appreciation to the organisers, guests, award recipients and participants for contributing to a successful event.\n\nOrganisers said the Annual Sessions 2026 reaffirm the Institute\u2019s commitment to promoting academic excellence, advancing research and nurturing the next generation of chemists in Sri Lanka.\n\nProf. Fazeeha Azmi becomes Lanka\u2019s first woman envoy to Iran\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
