    "chunk_size_bytes": 1251,
    "chunk_text": "IIHS marks 25 years with record graduation of over 650 healthcare professionals\n\nThe International Institute of Health Sciences (IIHS) celebrated a historic milestone on June 24, 2026, graduating over 650 healthcare professionals at a ceremony in Ragama. This year\u2019s event was particularly significant as it marked IIHS\u2019s 25th anniversary and the first-ever graduation of its Professional Bachelor\u2019s cohorts, with 227 students earning degrees in Nursing, Public Health, and Dental Therapy.\n\nChief Guest Professor Nophar Geifman of the University of Surrey urged graduates to embrace innovation and technology. Over the past quarter-century, IIHS has evolved into a \u201cGlobal Airport\u201d for healthcare careers, with its qualifications serving as a passport to international opportunities. The institution has trained over 5,000 professionals for Sri Lanka\u2019s workforce, while more than 2,500 alumni now work abroad. CEO Dr. Kithsiri Edirisinghe emphasized that IIHS certificates are transformative tools for global education, employment, and migration.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
