    "chunk_text": "The event saw the participation of Deputy Head of Central Office of Cultural and Ethical Progress of China Hu Kaihong, Speaker of the Parliament of Sri Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne, Deputy Minister of Education and Higher Education Madhura Senevirathne, China International Communications Group Vice President Yu Tao and the Communist Party of Sri Lanka General Secretary G. Weerasinghe among others.\n\nFollowing are excerpts of Ambassador Qi Zhenhong\u2019s speech at the ceremony.\n\nHu Kaihong delivered an in-depth and systematic exposition of the core tenets and rich essence of Xi Jinping: The Governance of China(Volume V), with a focus on China-Sri Lanka cooperation and exchanges. I believe that everyone here has gained a deeper understanding of the stances, viewpoints, as well as methods contained therein. I would like to take this opportunity to share a few reflections from my own study.\n\nThis work demonstrates that Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era is broad and profound, while keeping pace with the times. This thought is the Marxism of contemporary China and of the 21st century. It embodies the finest of Chinese culture and the Chinese spirit of our times, serving as a scientific guide for our endeavours to build a great country and advance national rejuvenation on all fronts through Chinese modernisation. Meanwhile, it has made a global contribution to people of all countries in enhancing cultural exchanges and mutual learning, jointly pursuing modernisation, and addressing the common challenges confronting humanity."
