    "md5": "c6f5e2863a60a0c5e8e23f5ce24424d6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1296,
    "chunk_text": "Dayasiri says he has stepped away from Facebook\n\nMain Opposition party, Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Dayasiri Jayasekara said he has temporarily stepped away from Facebook, saying the platform has become unproductive, while alleging that the Government is systematically targeting Opposition politicians.\n\nHe made the remarks in response to questions over his earlier comments on the possibility of toppling the Government by joining forces with what he described as \u201cthieves and robbers.\u201d\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t go on Facebook because it\u2019s full of fools. It is not a battleground where intelligent people fight. That\u2019s why I don\u2019t go there or even look at it,\u201d Jayasekara said.\n\nThe MP also claimed that the Government was arresting various individuals and attempting to discredit Opposition members by branding them with allegations ranging from racism and theft to drug-related offences and even terrorism.\n\nJayasekara argued that such allegations were being used to tarnish the reputations of politicians and questioned who would restore their names if the accusations were later found to be unfounded.\n\nHe also alleged that members of the joint Opposition were all being drawn into the same narrative, making it increasingly difficult for them to function effectively as an opposition."
