    "chunk_text": "IRD opens e-service portal for 2025/2026 income tax returns\n\nColombo, July 6 (Daily Mirror) - The Inland Revenue Department (IRD) has announced that its e-service platform is now open for the filing of Income Tax Returns for the Year of Assessment 2025/2026.\n\nAccording to a public notice issued by the department, taxpayers can now submit their returns electronically under several categories, including Corporate Income Tax (CIT), Partnership Income Tax (PIT), and Individual Income Tax (IIT), as well as the IIT Simplified Return.\n\nThe IRD said that all income tax returns for the relevant assessment year must be submitted electronically through its e-service platform on or before November 30, 2026.\n\nThe department has urged taxpayers to ensure timely submission of their returns to avoid any inconvenience and to comply with statutory requirements.\n\nThe IRD has also advised taxpayers to visit its official website for updated information and guidance on the filing process.\n\nThe announcement comes as the tax authority continues its efforts to expand digital services and improve tax administration under its \"Taxes \u2013 For a Better Future\" initiative.\n\nCOPF questions rationale behind high income tax rate for Port City employees\n\nBroaden tax base without counting too much on motor vehicle import duties - IMF"
