    "chunk_size_bytes": 1909,
    "chunk_text": "Uber arrives in Sri Lanka\u2019s gem capital\n\nUber, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading ride-hailing and delivery platform, announced the launch of Uber Eats and Uber Rides in Ratnapura, further expanding its footprint across the island.\n\nResidents and visitors can now access food, groceries, everyday essentials and reliable transportation through the Uber app, while local merchants, delivery partners and drivers gain new opportunities to grow and earn.\n\nWith Uber Eats now live across a broad coverage area in the district, the customers can order from iconic local favourites such as Tandoori, Thai Tanic, Garland and more, alongside grocery and retail partners, all delivered at the tap of a button.\n\nAt the same time, Uber Rides offers residents and visitors a convenient and affordable way to get around the entire Ratnapura district through a range of two, three and four-wheel options. Known as Sri Lanka\u2019s gem capital, Ratnapura is home to a vibrant community of entrepreneurs, merchants and small businesses, making it a natural next step in Uber\u2019s expansion across Sri Lanka.\n\nUber Sri Lanka Country Manager Delivery Varun Wijewardane said, \u201cRatnapura is home to a vibrant community of local businesses and entrepreneurs and we\u2019re excited to bring Uber Eats to the district. By connecting local merchants with more customers and creating flexible earning opportunities for delivery partners, we hope to make everyday convenience more accessible while supporting local economic growth.\u201d\n\nUber Sri Lanka Country Manager Mobility Kaushalya Gunaratne said, \u201cWe\u2019re excited to bring Uber Rides to Ratnapura and make reliable, affordable mobility available to more people across the district. This launch creates new earning opportunities for local drivers while giving residents and visitors access to convenient transportation backed by technology designed to make every trip safer and more seamless.\u201d"
  },
