    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Insurance Life declares record Rs.14.7bn bonus to policyholders\n\nSri Lanka Insurance Life (SLIC Life) has declared a record Rs.14.68 billion bonus to the policyholders for 2025, the highest annual life insurance bonus payout in Sri Lanka\u2019s insurance industry.\n\nThe latest declaration brings the company\u2019s cumulative bonus payouts since 2006 to Rs.131.28 billion, extending what it described as an unmatched record of delivering the industry\u2019s highest annual bonus over the years.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s life insurance sector continues to compete for long-term savings amid a gradually improving economic environment, with the policyholder bonuses remaining a key measure of the insurers\u2019 ability to generate investment returns.\n\nSLIC Life said its total asset base stood at Rs.275 billion at end-2025, while its life fund grew to Rs.247 billion, maintaining its position as the largest life fund in the industry.\n\nThe company also paid out more than Rs.16.2 billion in maturity benefits and claims during the year, averaging over Rs.1.35 billion a month, in addition to the annual bonus declaration.\n\nThe insurer reported a profit before tax of Rs.4.3 billion for 2025, while the gross written premium income rose 24 percent year-on-year to Rs.32.6 billion. The new business premium income recorded a stronger growth of 42 percent, reaching Rs.7.56 billion, reflecting the continued expansion of its customer base and policy sales.\n\nSLIC Life said the results were supported by prudent investment management and financial stability, despite the evolving economic conditions during the year."
