    "md5": "2858b4e0211cf614477095f480c37cde",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 837,
    "chunk_text": "Rohana Randombage appointed Director General of Sustainable Energy Authority\n\nColombo, July 7 (Daily Mirror) - Chartered Engineer Rohana Randombage has been appointed as the new Director General of the Sri Lanka Sustainable Energy Authority.\n\nHe received his appointment letter from Minister of Energy Anura Karunathilaka today (07).\n\nRandombage holds a degree in Mechanical Engineering from the University of Peradeniya and a Master\u2019s degree in Engineering Project Management from Auckland University of Technology. He also holds a Master\u2019s degree in Business Management.\n\nWith over 24 years of experience in local and international industries and businesses, Randombage is expected to lead the Sustainable Energy Authority in achieving its objectives as the country\u2019s key institution responsible for renewable energy development."
  },
  {
