    "chunk_text": "The Capital Goods sector emerged as the largest contributor to market turnover, generating LKR 0.48 Bn with 19.13 Mn shares traded. JKH.N led activity within the sector, recording LKR 0.30 Bn in turnover with 15.33 Mn shares traded. Crossing transactions accounted for LKR 0.55 Bn, representing 35% of total market turnover, with the largest crossing recorded in JKH.N amounting to LKR 0.26 Bn involving 13.20 Mn shares.\n\nAmong notable trades, SMOT.N recorded significant activity with a turnover of LKR 0.12 Bn on 0.10 Mn shares traded. However, the counter declined by 4.25% during the session, reflecting the cautious sentiment and selective profit-taking observed across the market. Overall, investors remained positioned cautiously as market participants awaited stronger earnings-driven signals to determine the next direction of the equity market."
