    "chunk_text": "Meanwhile, Capgemini Senior Test Automation Architect Neelam Pal addressed governance and ethics through her session \u2018Governance, Compliance and Ethical AI Assurance\u2019, highlighting the critical importance of accountability and compliance in AI-enabled systems.\n\nThe panel explored how AI is reshaping workforce dynamics while reinforcing the continued importance of human expertise in quality engineering.\n\nThe second day continued with equally impactful sessions. QA Roots founder Dr. Leonardo Lanni presented \u2018Reverse Mutation Testing\u2019, introducing innovative approaches to enhancing software reliability. This was followed by a leadership-focused session by Amazon Software Development Manager Dr. Chathuranga Manamendra, titled \u2018Operationalising AI in Software Delivery: A Leadership Playbook for Shared Quality, Speed and Governance\u2019, which explored the balance between innovation, governance and delivery speed.\n\nThe summit concluded with an interactive virtual workshop on \u2018Autonomous Testing\u2019, led by 3Pillar Global Senior Quality Lead Manager Kailash Pathak, offering the participants practical insights into the emerging AI-driven testing methodologies.\n\nSLASSCOM Quality Summit 2026 successfully created a dynamic platform for knowledge exchange, collaboration and forward-looking dialogue on the future of quality engineering. As AI adoption continues to accelerate across industries, the summit reinforced the critical message that QA professionals would remain central to ensuring trust, reliability, governance and human-centred innovation in the evolving digital economy."
