    "chunk_text": "CID completes probe into case against Ranil Wickremesinghe over London trip allegations\n\nColombo, July 8 (Daily Mirror) - The Criminal Investigation Department today informed Fort Magistrate Pasan Amarasena that it has concluded all investigations into the case filed against former President Ranil Wickremesinghe over allegations that he caused a loss of more than Rs. 16 million to the State.\n\nThe case relates to allegations that, during his tenure as President, Wickremesinghe undertook what has been described as a private visit to London to attend the graduation ceremony of his wife, Professor Maithree Wickremesinghe, resulting in a financial loss exceeding Rs. 16 million to the Government.\n\nAppearing on behalf of the CID, State Counsel Samadari Piyasena informed court that the investigation has been completed and the relevant extracts have been forwarded to the Attorney General for advice.\n\nThe Magistrate fixed the case for September 30 to obtain the Attorney General's instructions.\n\nCID team\u2019s trip to London for investigation cannot be justified: UNP\n\nInvestigation of alleged lavish spending for former President\u2019s London trip CID team\u2019s trip to London for investigation cannot be justified: UNP"
