    "md5": "5e348e9f0c67451207217dbe8e5bbd46",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1834,
    "chunk_text": "Smart Quest marks 20 years of people transformation with launch of \u2018The Growth Circle\u2019 and pre-launch of \u2018Rooted\u2019\n\nFounder and Director Andrea Jayatilleka handing over the first copy of \u2018Rooted\u2019 to her mother Roma Baldsing\n\nSmart Quest Ltd., marked its 20th anniversary with an intimate evening at Cinnamon Life, Colombo, bringing together clients, partners, faculty and leaders from more than 30 organisations across Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate landscape.\n\nThe milestone event reflected on two decades of leadership development, coaching and organisational transformation, while introducing Smart Quest\u2019s next chapter through the launch of The Growth Circle and the pre-launch edition of \u2018Rooted: In Stillness He Taught Me Everything About Leadership\u2019, the first book by Smart Quest Founder and Director Andrea Jayatilleka.\n\nThe evening opened with a welcome address by Chief Operating Officer Oshana Dias, setting the tone for a celebration that honoured Smart Quest\u2019s legacy while looking ahead to the evolving needs of leaders and teams in today\u2019s workplace.\n\nA key highlight of the event was the inaugural Growth Circle, a facilitated team experience designed to build trust, shared language and conscious leadership. Co-facilitated by Andrea Jayatilleka and Murshid Munshif, the session invited participants into a reflective conversation structured around five layers of growth, inspired by neurological levels of thinking and the concept of the \u201cStill Point\u201d referenced in \u2018Rooted\u2019.\n\nUsing picture cards, post-it notes and thread, participants explored questions around automatic responses, inner stillness, learning and conscious choice. The experience created space for open, honest conversation across industries, demonstrating the impact The Growth Circle is designed to bring into working teams."
  },
