    "chunk_text": "Using picture cards, post-it notes and thread, participants explored questions around automatic responses, inner stillness, learning and conscious choice. The experience created space for open, honest conversation across industries, demonstrating the impact The Growth Circle is designed to bring into working teams.\n\nThe evening also marked the pre-launch of \u2018Rooted: In Stillness He Taught Me Everything About Leadership\u2019, presented by Michelle de Silva. In a deeply personal moment, Andrea handed the first copy of the book to her mother, in tribute to the late J. Claude Baldsing, whose life and values inspired the book.\n\n\u2018Rooted\u2019 explores leadership through twenty reflections drawn from Andrea\u2019s father\u2019s quiet and deeply human way of leading. The book looks at principles such as competing only with yourself, leading with a big heart, showing up fully and continuing to grow, offering readers a personal yet practical reflection on the kind of leadership that leaves a lasting legacy.\n\nThe formal program concluded with reflections by Andrea Jayatilleka and Director Anil Bandara on Smart Quest\u2019s journey over the past twenty years, its relationships with clients and partners, and its continued belief that when people are developed well, organisations thrive.\n\nFollowing its successful inaugural edition, The Growth Circle is now available for working teams. Facilitated by Smart Quest\u2019s ICF-credentialed coaches and tailored to each team\u2019s context, the experience moves away from presentations and slides to create structured conversations that support trust, alignment and lasting momentum."
