    "md5": "9a403c884da6e9091276f69e1ddf5751",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1258,
    "chunk_text": "Locally too, BYD is become a fast favourite with Sri Lankan customers. Within nine months of vehicle imports resuming, BYD accounted for approximately 37 percent of all brand-new vehicle registrations and over 70 percent of electric vehicle registrations in Sri Lanka.\n\nDuring his visit, Liu engaged with the JKCG Auto team on BYD\u2019s continued plans to strengthen its presence in Sri Lanka, with discussions focused on sales, after-sales operations, charging infrastructure, technical expertise and the wider development of the country\u2019s NEV ecosystem. He also hosted an exclusive evening with DENZA customers, bringing together owners for an intimate dinner and a drive experience.\n\n\u201cBYD has changed the global conversation around new energy mobility. Similarly, in just one year, Sri Lanka too is waking up to the potential of a rapid NEV transition to completely transform mobility. We are therefore honoured to host Liu, whose visit further reinforces the confidence which BYD has placed in JKCG Auto, and in Sri Lanka. Together, we are building the local platform needed to support the next phase of NEV adoption, from market access and service readiness to charging and technical capability,\u201d John Keells CG Auto CEO, Charith Panditharatne said."
  },
