    "chunk_size_bytes": 930,
    "chunk_text": "It could have been nipped in the bud. Only if we had been given orders \u2013 Prison officer to Minister\n\nColombo, July 9 (Daily Mirror) - A prison officer told Justice Minister Harshana Nanayakkara yesterday that the Negombo prison unrest which claimed the lives of several prison officers and inmates could have been prevented had timely orders been issued to contain the situation.\n\nThe remarks were made when the Minister visited the funeral of the slain prison officers at the Welikada Prison premises yesterday. A video of the exchange has since gone viral on social media.\n\n\"It could have been nipped in the bud. Only if we had been given orders to stop the incident. Prisoners are also human,\" the officer is heard telling the Minister in the video.\n\nAnatomy of the Negombo prison riot: Government should fix the prison system without delay\n\n\u2018Prisoners are human beings:\u2019   The reality inside and outside the prison walls"
  },
