    "chunk_size_bytes": 1637,
    "chunk_text": "Negombo Prison declared crime scene, no longer suitable for housing inmates\n\nColombo, July 9 (Daily Mirror) - The prison authorities determined that the Negombo Prison premises, which were damaged during the recent unrest, were no longer suitable for housing inmates.\n\nThe Ministry of Justice and National Integration said that following the violence that unfolded at Negombo Prison on July 5 and 6, 2026, the prison was extensively damaged and officially classified as a crime scene.\n\n\"As a result, the majority of detainees were temporarily transferred to other prisons to ensure their safety while allowing investigators to conduct uninterrupted inquiries at the scene,\" the ministry said.\n\nEarlier, two Extraordinary Gazettes were issued designating the closed Mahamodara Hospital and the Old Bogambara premises as temporary prisons.\n\nThe ministry said the premises at Mahamodara and Old Bogambara have been designated as temporary prisons until extensive renovation work at Negombo Prison is completed, following the violent unrest that severely damaged the facility.\n\nThe ministry said the emergency transfers have further intensified overcrowding across the country's prison system. To address the increased inmate population and ensure prisoners' welfare, the ministry said that authorities identified the need for additional temporary accommodation.\n\n\u2018Prisoners are human beings:\u2019   The reality inside and outside the prison walls\n\nIt could have been nipped in the bud. Only if we had been given orders \u2013 Prison officer to Minister\n\nAnatomy of the Negombo prison riot: Government should fix the prison system without delay"
