    "chunk_text": "Special Ayurvedic medicines developed to combat dengue virus: Ayurveda Medical Officers\n\nColombo, July 10 (Daily Mirror) - The Government Ayurveda Medical Officers' Association (GAMOA) has claimed that special Ayurvedic medicines have been developed to combat the dengue virus.\n\nAddressing the media, GAMOA President Upul Konthasinghe said the medicines had been prepared to boost the immunity of the public and dengue patients.\n\nHe said the Western Province Ayurvedic Department had introduced a new medicine and was distributing it among households in the province as part of efforts to control the spread of dengue.\n\nThe department is also distributing dust used for mosquito fogging activities, he added.\n\nKonthasinghe requested the public not to discard the distributed items, noting that State funds had been spent on their production and distribution."
