    "language": "en",
    "md5": "0a1e0b4b9defd28146f1a68564971554",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1804,
    "chunk_text": "Uswatte Biscuits partners with Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage\u2019s Olympic journey\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s record-breaking javelin thrower, Rumesh Tharanga Pathirage, was honoured by Uswatte Biscuits Pvt Ltd, his official sponsor, at a special felicitation ceremony held on 22 June at Vinro Reception Hall, Kennanthudawa.\n\nHosted in Rumesh\u2019s hometown, the event brought together family members, relatives, friends, neighbours, and members of the local community who have supported and encouraged him throughout his journey, creating a heartfelt celebration among the people who have stood by him since childhood.\n\nThe event celebrated a series of historic performances that have elevated Sri Lanka\u2019s standing in international athletics and brought together sports officials, community leaders, supporters, and well-wishers to recognise Rumesh\u2019s remarkable rise on the global stage.\n\nRumesh\u2019s breakthrough season has seen him achieve unprecedented success. At the 2026 Rome Diamond League, he recorded a throw of 92.62 metres, setting a new Sri Lankan record while producing the world\u2019s leading javelin throw of the season. The achievement also placed him among the sport\u2019s all-time greats, ranking eighth in history at the time.\n\nHis impressive run continued with victory at the Ostrava Golden Spike athletics meet in the Czech Republic, where he secured first place with a throw of 86.57 metres against a strong international field. He further strengthened his credentials with another winning performance at the Diamond League meet in Doha, Qatar, contributing to his rise to World No. 2 in the global rankings.\n\nThese achievements have not only brought immense pride to Sri Lanka but have also demonstrated the country\u2019s ability to produce athletes capable of competing with the very best in the world."
  },
