    "chunk_text": "His impressive run continued with victory at the Ostrava Golden Spike athletics meet in the Czech Republic, where he secured first place with a throw of 86.57 metres against a strong international field. He further strengthened his credentials with another winning performance at the Diamond League meet in Doha, Qatar, contributing to his rise to World No. 2 in the global rankings.\n\nThese achievements have not only brought immense pride to Sri Lanka but have also demonstrated the country\u2019s ability to produce athletes capable of competing with the very best in the world.\n\nUswatte Biscuits, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s renowned biscuit manufacturers, has been a trusted household name for over 70 years. Guided by a commitment to quality, innovation, and affordability, the company continues to strengthen its presence both locally and internationally while contributing meaningfully to initiatives that inspire and uplift communities. The partnership with Rumesh reflects Uswatte Biscuits\u2019 enduring belief in recognising and supporting Sri Lankan talent capable of achieving excellence on the global stage.\n\nIn recognition of his historic accomplishments on the international stage, Uswatte Biscuits awarded a cash prize of Rs. 2.5 million to Rumesh. His coach, Tony Prasanna, was also honoured with a cash award of Rs. 500,000. The occasion also marked the beginning of a long-term partnership, with Uswatte Biscuits pledging its continued support towards Rumesh\u2019s journey to the 2028 Olympic Games in Los Angeles. The company reaffirmed its commitment to standing alongside the athlete as he pursues his ultimate goal of winning an Olympic medal for Sri Lanka."
