    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka attends 9th\u00a0ESCAP Committee Session on Environment and Development\n\nThe Sri Lankan delegation, led by Environment Deputy Minister Anton Jayakody actively participated in the Ninth Session of the Committee on Environment and Development (CED-9) of the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (ESCAP), held in Bangkok from 1 to 3 July 2026.\n\nThroughout the three-day session, the Sri Lankan delegation made substantive contributions to the Committee\u2019s deliberations, participated in high-level bilateral and regional engagements, and highlighted the Government\u2019s commitment to strengthening environmental governance, climate resilience and sustainable development through enhanced regional cooperation. Sri Lanka\u2019s active participation was widely appreciated by delegates and development partners, reaffirming the country\u2019s constructive role in advancing the regional environmental agenda.\n\nUnder Agenda Item 4 on the Report on the Work of the Technical Expert Group on Environment and Development, Sri Lanka Ambassador and Permanent Representative to ESCAP Wijayanthi Edirisinghe delivered Sri Lanka\u2019s statement, reaffirming the country\u2019s commitment to addressing the triple planetary crisis of climate change, biodiversity loss and pollution. The Ambassador highlighted the importance of localising climate action through stronger engagement of subnational governments in implementing Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) and welcomed ESCAP\u2019s continued technical support and regional cooperation to strengthen urban resilience, climate financing and sustainable development."
  },
