    "md5": "b152946a41e2b152ce447d0b5b80f9de",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "Dialog Enterprise, NCE renew strategic  partnership to accelerate digital transformation\n\nFrom left: Dialog Enterprise Head of SME Products, Converged Connectivity Sameera Wijerathna, NCE Chief Operating Officer Inok Perera, Secretary General/CEO Shiham Marikar, Dialog Enterprise Group Chief Officer Navin Pieris and Vice President/Head of Innovation and Platform Business Viranga Seneviratne\n\nDialog Enterprise, the corporate solutions arm of Dialog Axiata PLC and Sri Lanka\u2019s number one ICT solutions provider, has renewed its strategic partnership with the National Chamber of Exporters of Sri Lanka (NCE), reaffirming its commitment to empowering Sri Lankan exporters with advanced digital technologies, industry expertise, and innovation-driven solutions.\n\nThe renewed partnership builds on a successful collaboration established in 2025, under which Dialog Enterprise served as the official Digital Technology Partner of NCE. Through this partnership, both organisations have worked closely to enhance the digital capabilities of Sri Lankan exporters by facilitating access to cutting-edge ICT solutions, knowledge-sharing initiatives, and technology-led business transformation programs. As part of the renewed collaboration, Dialog Enterprise will continue to support NCE and its membership base with a comprehensive portfolio of Digital Transformation tools including converged connectivity, cloud services, cybersecurity, data analytics, artificial intelligence, and Internet of Things (IoT) technologies. The partnership will also facilitate educational forums, industry workshops, and expert-led sessions designed to help exporters navigate evolving global market demands and accelerate their Digital Transformation journeys specially focusing on the Aspiring Exporters who are Small and Medium Entrepreneurs (SME)."
  },
