    "chunk_size_bytes": 1698,
    "chunk_text": "On one holiday, I planned a trip back to Sri Lanka, while David arranged to return to India. We flew from Dhahran to Bahrain and planned to get our connecting flights from there. But, true to form, Dhahran airport caused long delays, and by the time we landed in Bahrain, my flight to Colombo had departed. David suggested that I fly to Bombay (now Mumbai) with him, stay there overnight, and fly to Colombo on the following day. I agreed.\n\nIt was clear to me that he was expecting a bribe, as he said \u201cI am just doing my duty. I don\u2019t expect anything from you.\u201d I told him that I would not bribe him anyway, and asked him to check my other bag as well. He stopped hassling me and let me go. In those days, Bombay was a very crowded city filled with heavy traffic and pollution. Beggars were everywhere, and the roads were in terrible condition. Now it has been transformed into a modern city full of high rise buildings, as I saw in a recent visit.\n\nThat night, we stayed at the home of David\u2019s relative. Before going there, despite David\u2019s objection, I bought food and drink to take along for dinner. Next morning I got ready to go to the airport by taxi. In my pocket, I had two brand-new, gold rimmed Parker pens, which I planned to gift to my relatives in Sri Lanka. A young woman in the house asked for my pen to write down an address and I obliged. Later, her sister asked me for the other pen, and I could not refuse. After a while, since I did not get my pens back, I assumed that they had forgotten to return them. So I asked one girl for the pen and she told me that she couldn\u2019t find it. I gave up the hope of getting my pens back, left for the airport, and reached Colombo."
