    "chunk_size_bytes": 1218,
    "chunk_text": "In AGT systems, the vehicles move on elevated guideways in existing transportation corridors. The analysis and design of AGT systems was comprehensively presented in this second book. My effort in producing these two technical books became successful, and the books are available in the market even now (see figure below).\n\nWhile in Cambridge, my family and I used to go to Abbotsford in my Lada Riva car. My cousin Dudley Talawila lived in Abbotsford, which is about two hours south of Cambridge. Dudley was a fun-loving character who to our great sadness died young, leaving a wife, two sons and a daughter. They were all very hospitable to us when we visited their home.\n\nDudley was a Civil Engineer. In one visit to Abbotsford, we were watching a video cassette that Dudley had received from Sri Lanka (this happened in 1987). It contained several programs recorded from a Sri Lankan government TV channel. One of the recordings was on an Avurudu Kumari contest which we particularly enjoyed. Dudley who had not seen the video before said he\u2019d pick the winner and chose the girl who greeted the chief guest and helped him to light the traditional oil lamp. She was indeed the winner but Dudley felt undeservedly."
