    "chunk_size_bytes": 1326,
    "chunk_text": "Ultimately, meritocracy means selecting the right person for the right job through transparent, objective, evidence-based assessment.\n\n\u00b7 Integrity, accountability, and independent oversight throughout recruitment and promotion.\n\nPublic appointments must never become rewards for political loyalty, family influence, or personal favour. Every public office should have legally defined selection criteria, transparent recruitment processes, independent oversight, and meaningful accountability.\n\nStrong institutions are built by competent people. Competent people inspire public confidence. Public confidence attracts investment, strengthens democracy, improves public services, and drives sustainable economic growth.\n\nMeritocracy is not about creating an elite class. It is about ensuring that every citizen has a fair opportunity to develop their talents and that every important position is entrusted to the individual best qualified to fulfil its responsibilities.\n\nOnly then can Sri Lanka unlock the full potential of its people and build a society where opportunity depends not on whom you know, but on what you can contribute.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
