    "md5": "7800a0ab7e76d6f26e68c077975e0b33",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 556,
    "chunk_text": "Irrigation Department urges water conservation amid El Ni\u00f1o concerns\n\nColombo, July 11 (Daily Mirror) - The Irrigation Department has urged the public, including farmers, to use water sparingly in view of a possible El Ni\u00f1o situation in the future.\n\nDirector of Water Management H. M. P. S. D. Herath said that 80 reservoirs currently hold around 48% of their total capacity, adding that the available water is expected to be sufficient.\n\nHe highlighted the importance of conserving water resources to ensure availability during potential dry conditions."
