    "md5": "a2a25c5670a37faf372977f8266cf67c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1834,
    "chunk_text": "Bank of Ceylon pioneers contactless payments with launch of \u2018BOC Flex \u2013 Tap & Pay\u2019\n\nThe Bank of Ceylon (BOC) has officially launched \u201cBOC Flex \u2013 Tap & Pay,\u201d marking Sri Lanka\u2019s first mobile banking wallet-based contactless payment solution.\n\nIntroduced on July 9, 2026, this landmark digital milestone builds upon the bank\u2019s next-generation \u201cBOC Flex\u201d internet and mobile banking platform, which originally debuted in March 2025.\n\nThe launch event was attended by key state officials, including the Minister of Labour, the Deputy Minister of Finance, and the Minister of Digital Economy, alongside representatives from the Central Bank of Sri Lanka and Mastercard, highlighting the national significance of the rollout.\n\nIntegrated directly within the existing BOC Flex mobile app, the Tap & Pay solution combines a secure digital wallet with advanced virtual card technology. This allows users to conduct fast, secure, and seamless cardless transactions at any Near-Field Communication (NFC)-enabled Point-of-Sale (POS) terminal, as well as across online merchant networks.\n\nFlexible Wallet Management: Users can transfer funds from their main BOC accounts to the wallet to pay utility bills, transfer money, or settle credit card balances. An automated \u201cAuto Top-Up\u201d feature instantly replenishes the wallet from a linked account if balances run low.\n\nVirtual Card Controls: Customers can generate up to three virtual cards simultaneously. The system includes robust self-service features allowing users to instantly suspend, reactivate, or change the primary funding source of their cards on the go.\n\nNational Alignment: The initiative directly supports the government\u2019s Digital Economy agenda, aiming to drive financial inclusion and accelerate the domestic transition toward a modern, cash-lite society."
