    "md5": "cc074fea7c641fb3868a2509c4a97114",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 823,
    "chunk_text": "Six Tamil-speaking parties to unveil common political platform\n\nTamil-speaking political parties will today (13) announce a joint agreement to work together on matters of common concern, signalling a coordinated political approach on key national issues.\n\nThe parties said they have reached a consensus to collaborate on issues of mutual interest at the current juncture and will outline the agreement at a media briefing scheduled for today (13).\n\nThe alliance comprises the All Ceylon Makkal Congress (ACMC), Ceylon Workers\u2019 Congress (CWC), Democratic Tamil National Alliance (DTNA), Ilankai Tamil Arasu Kadchi (ITAK), Sri Lanka Muslim Congress (SLMC) and the Tamil Progressive Alliance (TPA).\n\nThe parties are expected to provide further details on the scope and objectives of the initiative during the media briefing."
  },
