    "md5": "431fc07977972270c0dc8a4866e918b1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1722,
    "chunk_text": "DFCC Bank-MyFees.lk advance digital payments across education sector\n\nDFCC Bank Director and Chief Executive Officer Thimal Perera exchanges the agreement with MyFees.lk Chief Executive Officer Faiq Faiz in the presence of (from left) DFCC Bank Assistant Manager Merchant Acquiring Jude Amarasekera, DFCC Bank Senior Manager Merchant Acquiring Chrishan Jayamanne and MyFees.lk Business Development Manager Kevin Perera\n\nDFCC Bank PLC has entered into a strategic partnership with MyFees.lk, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading education-focused digital payment platform, to strengthen digital payment capabilities across the country\u2019s education sector and improve payment convenience for institutions, students and families.\n\nThe partnership reflects the growing digitalisation of education-related financial transactions, as schools, higher education institutions, professional bodies and training providers increasingly seek more efficient, transparent and secure ways to manage fee collection and payments.\n\nBy combining DFCC Bank\u2019s digital banking capabilities, including its internet payment gateway and payment acceptance solutions, with MyFees.lk\u2019s specialised education payment platform, the collaboration aims to simplify the payment processes while reducing administrative complexity for educational institutions.\n\nDFCC Bank Director and CEO Thimal Perera said, \u201cAt its heart, this partnership is about making life easier for families and strengthening the institutions that support learning. By combining financial services with digital innovation, we are helping create a more connected education ecosystem that reduces complexity, improves accessibility and delivers meaningful value to the communities we serve.\u201d"
  },
