    "chunk_text": "Hemas Hospitals wins 30 Quality Awards\n\nHemas Hospitals & Laboratory Chain celebrates 30 awards at NCQP 2026, honouring the innovation and dedication of their teams in delivering better healthcare every day\n\nHemas Hospitals & Laboratory Chain has set a new national benchmark in healthcare quality, winning 30 awards at National Convention on Quality and Productivity (NCQP) 2026 \u2014 the highest number of awards won by a single hospital in the country.\n\nThe achievement, comprising 22 Gold awards, seven Silver awards and one Bronze award, reflects Hemas Hospitals\u2019 leadership in driving quality standards, patient safety, operational excellence and continuous improvement across Sri Lanka\u2019s healthcare sector.\n\nWhat makes this milestone especially significant is that every quality improvement project presented by Hemas Hospitals & Laboratory Chain received national recognition. This demonstrates not only the strength of individual initiatives but also the depth of the organisation\u2019s quality culture across its hospital and laboratory network.\n\nOrganised annually by the Sri Lanka Association for the Advancement of Quality and Productivity, NCQP recognises organisations that deliver measurable improvements through quality management and productivity initiatives. The 2026 convention was held under the theme \u2018People-Driven Quality and Productivity for a Resilient Sri Lanka\u2019, highlighting the importance of employee-led innovation in building stronger organisations and industries.\n\nThe 30 award-winning projects addressed real, practical challenges in healthcare delivery. These included reducing emergency treatment delays, improving outpatient physiotherapy preparation times, enhancing patient communication, strengthening medication management, improving medical documentation, reducing needle-stick injuries, improving dialysis services, strengthening call centre performance, increasing energy efficiency and improving waste segregation."
