    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3517b7491fcf8ce7c67fcf026569cb02",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1943,
    "chunk_text": "Union Assurance wins Second Celent Model Insurer Award\n\nUnion Assurance has been recognised as a Model Insurer for Customer Experience at the Celent Model Insurer Awards 2026, setting a global benchmark for the Life Insurance industry and showcasing leadership in technology-driven transformation.\n\nWidely regarded as one of the insurance industry\u2019s most respected recognitions, the annual Model Insurer Awards by Celent, a global research and advisory firm for the financial services industry, recognise insurance carriers for outstanding technology initiatives that demonstrate clear business impact, innovation, and technology or implementation excellence.\n\nThe recognition was awarded for Union Assurance\u2019s Connected Life Initiative, a transformative programme delivering a seamless, end-to-end digital experience across the customer lifecycle. It spans insurance education, purchase, underwriting, servicing, and claims, alongside integrated wellness solutions that support customer well-being.\n\nPowered by the Union Assurance Clicklife App, Sri Lanka\u2019s first and most comprehensive digital Life Insurance ecosystem, the initiative is redefining how customers access, manage, and engage with Life Insurance empowering them to better protect what matters most.\n\nThe programme integrates co-banking data prefill, a digital medical results exchange platform, and automated underwriting to deliver near-instant protection with zero physical paperwork.\n\nCustomers benefit from 24/7 self-service supported by agent-assisted digital channels and can submit claims in under two minutes, with real-time tracking at every step. Extending beyond transactions, the initiative also introduces Clicklife Suwamaga+, an AI-powered wellness ecosystem offering nutrition tracking, activity monitoring, gamified health challenges, and CSR-linked health awareness, extending the role of financial protection seamlessly into customers\u2019 everyday lives."
  },
