    "md5": "08e7d622b26a8db97d0ef11ff8c2b6fb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 641,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s oldest woman passes away at 114\n\nColombo, July 13 (Daily Mirror) - Punchage Kalumenike, a resident of Sangili Kanadarawa in the Anuradhapura District, who was widely recognized as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s oldest living women, has passed away at the age of 114.\n\nBorn on July 4, 1912, Kalumenike recently celebrated her 114th birthday alongside her family. According to reports, her health had declined following a fall earlier this year, which necessitated a surgical procedure.\n\nShe was a mother to 12 children and was blessed to see an extensive lineage that included an impressive 325 descendants, including great-grandchildren."
