    "chunk_text": "MBAPP\u00c9 vs YAMAL! World Cup Final Spot on the Line\n\nJuly.14 (Mirror Sports) - The FIFA World Cup 2026 reaches its biggest showdown yet as France and Spain clash in a blockbuster semi-final with a place in the final at stake. Kylian Mbapp\u00e9's free-scoring France face Lamine Yamal's European champions in a battle between two of football's brightest stars and leading title contenders.\n\nFrance and Spain meet in the first FIFA World Cup 2026 semi-final at Dallas Stadium in Arlington, Texas, with kick-off scheduled for 12:30 a.m. SLST on Wednesday, July 15.\n\nLed by Golden Boot frontrunner Kylian Mbapp\u00e9, France have powered into the last four after victories over Norway, Senegal, Iraq, Sweden, Paraguay and Morocco. Spain, inspired by teenage sensation Lamine Yamal, have defeated Saudi Arabia, Uruguay, Austria, Portugal and Belgium to continue their impressive march toward the title.\n\nThe semi-final brings together two of the tournament's strongest sides. France boast one of the competition's most explosive attacks, while Spain have built their campaign on disciplined defending, midfield dominance and clinical finishing.\n\nThe winners will advance to the FIFA World Cup 2026 final, where they will face either Argentina or England, setting the stage for another unforgettable chapter in World Cup history.\n\nFINAL FOUR CONFIRMED! Only four World Cup Finals are Still Possible"
