    "md5": "b22d2e7d23854df321415aa21c50782a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1738,
    "chunk_text": "Lanka IOC PLC successfully concludes 24th Annual General Meeting\n\nLanka IOC PLC successfully conducted its 24th Annual General Meeting (AGM) on 09 July 2026 , reaffirming the Company\u2019s commitment to sustainable growth, sound corporate governance, and long-term value creation for its shareholders and stakeholders.\n\nThe AGM was attended in person by Chairman Anuj Jain, Managing Director K. Raghu in the presence of Directors of the Board Saumitra P. Srivastava, Rajesh Singh,\u00a0 Manil Jayesinghe, S Renganathan through VC and Company Secretary.\n\nDuring the AGM the Board presented the Company\u2019s Annual Report and Audited Financial Statements for the financial year ended 31 March 2026, providing shareholders with a comprehensive overview of the Company\u2019s financial performance, operational achievements, strategic initiatives, and future growth plans.\n\nAddressing the shareholders, the Chairman highlighted the LIOC\u2019s ability to successfully navigate a challenging operating environment characterised by global geopolitical uncertainties, volatility in international energy markets, and evolving domestic economic conditions. Despite these challenges, Lanka IOC continued to ensure the uninterrupted supply of petroleum products across Sri Lanka while strengthening its operational capabilities and expanding its business portfolio.\n\nThe Company also outlined its strategic priorities, including investments in digital transformation, expansion of its retail network, growth of the lubricants and petrochemical businesses, enhancement of operational efficiencies, and the pursuit of sustainable energy opportunities, including electric vehicle charging infrastructure and renewable energy projects through strategic partnerships."
  },
