    "chunk_size_bytes": 1667,
    "chunk_text": "Cardinal calling the shots in military appointments, charges Opposition MP\n\nColombo, July 14 (Daily Mirror) - There is a sinister move by the government to extend the term of the current army commander until January 2028 following the request of the Archbishop of Colombo Cardinal Malcolm Ranjith, Opposition MP Chamara Sampath Dassanayake charged.\n\n\u201cThe term of the current army commander ended on July 2 2026. There is a move to extend his term further until January 2028. A number of senior army officers, including Nilantha Premaratne will be overlooked when extending the term of the current army commander. The one who will take over from the current army commander in 2028 will be a person surnamed Fernando. This is being done following the request of Cardinal Ranjith,\u201d the MP said during a seminar organised by the joint opposition.\n\n\u201cThose in the government meet Mahanayake Theras once in three months. However, it seems that Cardinal has a say in appointments. The people who are appointed to posts such as army commander and the CID chief is decided upon by the Cardinal. It is a good thing that the Sri Lankan cardinal did not become the Pope. Sri Lanka would have become another Vatican if cardinal Ranjith was elected pope,\u201d the MP added.\n\nHitting out at the church further, Mr Dassanayake charged that some catholic priests had lodged in holiday resorts run by the Army in Batticaloa recently and had enjoyed luxury.\n\nMP Dassanayake was critical of Minister Lalkatha, who was reported to have said Sri Lankans are consuming too much rice. \u201cI would like to ask the minister as to what we should eat instead of rice,\u201d he said sarcastically."
