    "md5": "402596d691ce7b322941155aa29e2eeb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "Bogawantalawa Tea enters Saudi Arabia\u2019s Tamimi hypermarket chain\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s premium Bogawantalawa Tea was officially launched at Tamimi Markets, one of Saudi Arabia\u2019s leading hypermarket chains, at a ceremony held in Riyadh on 9 July, marking a further expansion of premium Ceylon Tea in the Kingdom.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to Saudi Arabia, Ameer Ajwad, inaugurated the launch and said Saudi Arabia remains one of the most important export destinations for Ceylon Tea. He noted that the introduction of Bogawantalawa Tea represented another milestone in strengthening the presence of premium Sri Lankan tea in the Saudi market.\n\nThe Ambassador thanked Tamimi Markets for providing a platform to introduce premium Sri Lankan tea to Saudi consumers and proposed establishing a dedicated \u201cSri Lanka Corner\u201d at the supermarket chain to showcase a wider range of premium Sri Lankan products. He also highlighted the steady growth of Sri Lankan exports to Saudi Arabia in recent years and stressed the need to further diversify the country\u2019s export basket.\n\nBogawantalawa Tea Ceylon Co-Chairman Lalith Kumar Ambani said the company\u2019s Ceylon Tea Gardens brand is internationally recognised for its quality, distinctive flavour, freshness and more than a century of heritage.\n\nHe said the partnership with Tamimi Markets would enable consumers across Saudi Arabia to enjoy authentic premium Ceylon Tea.\n\nDirector and Chief Executive Officer Almas Marikkar outlined the company\u2019s diverse product portfolio and its commitment to corporate social responsibility through the welfare and development of estate communities. Marketing Manager for the Middle East and Asia Anne Ranasinghe presented the brand\u2019s history and heritage during the event.\n\nRepresentatives of Tamimi Markets, including Regional Senior Manager Ayham Nasser, Business Development Director Bruce Bostwick, and Category Manager Husnee Thasim, reaffirmed the retailer\u2019s commitment to offering customers high-quality international brands."
