    "md5": "ac864e476266e8656d934d438d6454bc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1847,
    "chunk_text": "Yamaha opens flagship concept showroom in Borella\n\nAssociated Motorways (Private) Limited (AMW), the official distributor for Yamaha, has opened Yamaha\u2019s flagship Concept Showroom in Sri Lanka at Borella, marking the brand\u2019s 45-year presence in the country while introducing a redesigned retail destination that brings together the brand\u2019s motorcycles, scooters, Outboard Motors (OBM), water vehicles, genuine spare parts, accessories and official Yamaha merchandise under one roof.\n\nYamaha\u2019s long-standing Borella location has been transformed into a modern concept showroom that offers a more engaging and customer-focused retail experience while reflecting the brand\u2019s global identity.\n\nCommenting on the opening, a representative from Yamaha marketing team at Associated Motorways (Private) Limited said, \u201cThe new Borella Concept Showroom embodies the modern Yamaha experience we want our customers to have. It is a destination where customers can interact with the entire Yamaha brand, not just a place to purchase a motorcycle or scooter. We remain dedicated to creating retail spaces that reflect the quality of our products while meeting the growing expectations of customers as we strengthen our presence in Sri Lanka.\u201d\n\nThe opening ceremony was attended by distinguished local and international guests, including Naoaki Kamoshida, Charg\u00e9 d\u2019Affaires ad interim of Japan to Sri Lanka, Embassy of Japan; Jorge Navea, Chief Executive Officer \u2013 Automotive, Al Futtaim; Antoine Barthes, Vice President \u2013 Automotive, Al Futtaim; Hajime Aota, Chairman, Yamaha Motor India Group; Toshiro Yagi, Executive General Manager, Yamaha Motor Company; Hideki Yamanaka, Group Manager, Yamaha Motor Company; Jawahar Ganesh, Managing Director, Associated Motorways (Private) Limited; and Sri Lankan motorsport legend Dilantha Malagamuwa."
