    "md5": "8583a9dd567b0df849141a0c0bf1531f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1828,
    "chunk_text": "OPA\u2019s 39th Annual Conference to map out structural path beyond recovery\n\nThe Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA) has announced its flagship 39th Annual Conference, scheduled to take place on August 11 and 12, at the Cinnamon Grand Colombo.\n\nAs the apex representative body governing 52 member associations across 34 professional disciplines\u2014including law, medicine, engineering, accountancy, and banking\u2014the OPA represents a collective network of more than 60,000 professionals nationwide.\n\nThis year\u2019s summit marks a crucial milestone as the organization enters its second half-century of public service. The inaugural ceremony will be graced by Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya as the Chief Guest, alongside British High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Andrew Patrick as the Guest of Honour, setting the stage for a critical national dialogue on the country\u2019s future development trajectories.\n\nGrounded on the timely theme of \u201cEnvisioning Sri Lanka: Beyond Recovery,\u201d the conference shifts the national focus away from temporary crisis management toward sustainable, long-term economic transformation. While recent macroeconomic indicators point to stabilizing conditions, including a notable 5.1 percent economic growth rate recorded in the first quarter, professional bodies emphasize that simple recovery from the recent economic debacle is insufficient. The upcoming forum acts as a strategic platform to dissect persistent structural constraints, fiscal management issues, and external dependencies that leave the country\u2019s small open economy vulnerable to global shocks. The overarching objective is to transition from reactive crisis mitigation to proactive risk management and inclusive development, ensuring that the benefits of national progress reach all segments of society."
