    "chunk_text": "Grounded on the timely theme of \u201cEnvisioning Sri Lanka: Beyond Recovery,\u201d the conference shifts the national focus away from temporary crisis management toward sustainable, long-term economic transformation. While recent macroeconomic indicators point to stabilizing conditions, including a notable 5.1 percent economic growth rate recorded in the first quarter, professional bodies emphasize that simple recovery from the recent economic debacle is insufficient. The upcoming forum acts as a strategic platform to dissect persistent structural constraints, fiscal management issues, and external dependencies that leave the country\u2019s small open economy vulnerable to global shocks. The overarching objective is to transition from reactive crisis mitigation to proactive risk management and inclusive development, ensuring that the benefits of national progress reach all segments of society.\n\nSpeaking at the media briefing ahead of the event, OPA office bearers highlighted that the collective expertise harbored within the institution is systematically channelled directly to state planners. Rather than acting as a mere talking shop, the OPA leverages its multi-disciplinary pool of experts to draft actionable concept papers and technical frameworks. The upcoming conference, which anticipates over 250 high-level participants for its technical sessions alone, will culminate in a comprehensive policy document handed directly to government ministries.\n\nLed by the annual conference committee, including President Jayantha Gallehewa, President-Elect Tisara De Silva, and General Secretary Ravi Rupasinghe, the OPA intends to utilize this upcoming summit to forge practical pathways, driving the nation toward a resilient, progressive, and structurally sound economic future."
