    "chunk_id": "2026-07-14-dailymirrorlk-f470d314-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b61e74951ede113039184f25f795b33f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1990,
    "chunk_text": "First Capital Holdings-First Capital Treasuries achieve verified GHG emissions certification for FY 2025/26\n\nFirst Capital Holdings PLC, together with First Capital Treasuries PLC, has successfully obtained the Greenhouse Gas (GHG) Emissions Verification Certificate for the financial year 2025/26 (April 01, 2025 \u2013 March 31, 2026), issued by Sri Lanka Climate Fund (Pvt.) Ltd, under the Environment Ministry (Opinion No: SLCF/CFP/0581, dated June 04, 2026).\n\nThe GHG statement has been independently verified in accordance with the specifications of ISO 14064-3:2019, complying with the requirements of ISO 14064-1:2018, with a reasonable level of assurance.\n\nAs a capital markets institution, financed emissions represent a significant component of the company\u2019s overall emissions footprint.\n\nFirst Capital is progressing towards measuring and incorporating financed emissions into its GHG inventory. Emissions arising from investment portfolios have been excluded from the defined organisational boundary of assessment.\n\nThe verified emissions for the financial year 2025/26 were 194 tonnes of CO\u2082 equivalent for First Capital Holdings and 54 tonnes of CO\u2082 equivalent for First Capital Treasuries.\n\nFirst Capital\u2019s sustainability journey is anchored in the belief that long-term success stems from empowering people through financial literacy and responsible social and environmental practices. At the heart of its agenda is a commitment to advancing financial stability, enabling individuals and communities to make informed financial decisions, build economic strength and contribute meaningfully to national development.\n\nThis core focus is complemented by initiatives in community engagement, climate action and environmental protection, ensuring a balanced approach to sustainable growth. Aligned with SLFRS S2 and global best practices, First Capital champions programmes that promote inclusive progress, sustainable development and long-term well-being across Sri Lanka."
  },
