    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "Baby Cheramy and Clogard among SL\u2019s Favourite Product Brands in PepperCube T25\n\nHemas Consumer Brands\u2019 two most trusted household names Baby Cheramy and Clogard have been recognised among Sri Lanka\u2019s Favourite Product Brands in a survey conducted by PepperCube Consultants and\u00a0published by LMD.\n\nThe results of the T25 favourite products/service brands are based on a monthly sample of 1,000 and reported cumulatively from 12,000 respondents at an all-island level over a 12-month period (May 2025 \u2013 April 2026).\n\nThe survey captures 12,000 consumer responses annually, based on unprompted nominations for favourite product and service brands, with the Top 25 brands in each category selected and listed alphabetically.\n\nThe inclusion of both Baby Cheramy and Clogard in the 2026 survey reflects their strong presence in Sri Lankan households and the deep trust they have earned through decades of consistently delivering products that meet the evolving needs of consumers.\n\nBaby Cheramy\u2019s recognition among Sri Lanka\u2019s Favourite Product Brands reflects consumer preference for the brand among families. In addition, being listed in the LMD as the \u2018Most Loved Brand\u2019 along with being named the \u2018Best of Best\u2019 Brand reinforces Baby Cheramy\u2019s position at the forefront of the baby\u00a0care category.\n\nHemas Consumer Brands General Manager Marketing Tulsi Liyanage stated, \u201cBeing recognised as a Favourite Product Brand in the PepperCube T25 Survey is a special honour. Our brands have nurtured babies across many generations and we are deeply grateful for that emotional connection which drives us to continually innovate and deliver superior value through trusted, high-quality products that evolve alongside the changing needs of families.\u201d\n\nSimilarly, Clogard\u2019s recognition in the T25 PepperCube Survey reflects the confidence Sri Lankan households continue to place in the brand and its role in promoting a complete oral care routine that delivers better oral health to Sri Lankan families."
